{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_1bf21575a3be",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "The default assignment `frame_len_valid_next = 1'b0` unconditionally clears the valid pulse in the same cycle it is asserted. Changing the default to `frame_len_valid_reg` (retain state) preserves the 1-cycle pulse until the next combinational evaluation, matching the observed trace where `frame_len_valid` stays asserted for exactly one cycle."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_c1e6cd26e2ef",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 98,
      "mechanism": "The loop counts bits for every `i` where `tkeep` matches the contiguous mask. At cycle 5, `tkeep=1` matches both `i=0` (mask 0) and `i=1` (mask 1), so `bit_cnt` becomes 1 instead of 0, adding an extra byte. Guarding the equality with `(!frame_reg)` ensures the count only runs when starting a new frame (`frame_reg==0`), preventing spurious increments on continuation cycles."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_e75a1cff7e0b",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 84,
      "mechanism": "The `if (monitor_axis_tlast)` block executes even when `tready=0` because the outer qualifier only checks `tready && tvalid`. Adding `&& (monitor_axis_tready)` makes the frame-termination logic (valid pulse, frame_reg clear) conditional on a *ready* transfer, which is the protocol requirement: a frame ends only on a valid AND ready last beat."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_4ac42f1009e7",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 95,
      "mechanism": "The `if (KEEP_ENABLE)` block runs on every ready/valid beat, but `frame_len_next` should only be reset to 0 at frame start (`!frame_reg`). Qualifying with `&& (!frame_reg)` prevents re-initializing the accumulator mid-frame, avoiding double-count or reset glitches during multi-beat frames."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_1e51d2e21710",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "The outer `if (tready && tvalid)` processes beats even when already inside a frame (`frame_reg==1`). Adding `&& (!frame_reg)` restricts entry actions (frame start, length reset) to the first beat of a frame, aligning with the spec that only the first enabled beat of a frame initializes the counter."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_5e3af25f023e",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 81,
      "mechanism": "After `frame_len_valid_reg` pulses high, `frame_len_reg` holds the reported length until explicitly cleared. Inserting `if (frame_len_valid_reg) frame_len_next = 0;` at the top of the combinational block resets the accumulator immediately after the valid cycle, preventing the stale length from contaminating the next frame’s count."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_a0ac38b154f7",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 95,
      "mechanism": "When `rst` is asserted mid-frame, `KEEP_ENABLE` logic should be disabled to avoid counting during reset. Qualifying with `&& (!rst)` suppresses the bit-count adder during active reset, ensuring `frame_len` stays at 0 while `rst=1`."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_158c82e15fb9",
      "failure_port": "frame_len",
      "source_line": 88,
      "mechanism": "The `else if (!frame_reg)` block starts a new frame on any ready/valid beat when not already in a frame. Adding `&& (!monitor_axis_tlast)` prevents treating a single-beat frame (tlast=1) as both start and continuation, avoiding double execution of start logic and the terminator logic in the same cycle."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The discovery trace shows `frame_len` = 3 at cycle 5 instead of 1. Root causes are: (1) `frame_len_valid_next` default 0 kills the valid pulse in the same cycle (patch_1bf21575a3be); (2) bit-count loop matches multiple `i` for `tkeep=1` because no `!frame_reg` guard (patch_c1e6cd26e2ef); (3) frame termination logic runs without `tready` (patch_e75a1cff7e0b); (4) `KEEP_ENABLE` adder runs mid-frame without `!frame_reg` (patch_4ac42f1009e7); (5) outer qualifier lacks `!frame_reg` so start logic re-triggers (patch_1e51d2e21710); (6) no post-valid reset of `frame_len_next` (patch_5e3af25f023e); (7) reset assertion leaks into bit-count (patch_a0ac38b154f7); (8) single-beat frame start/end collision (patch_158c82e15fb9). Patches are ordered by directness to the observed mismatch at cycle 5."
}
